{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbmqFBW7CdMon9axpbcy", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I haven't made the change. A plain retry here could charge customers twice.\n\n**Why:** `finalize()` POSTs to the ledger without an idempotency key. The project has a hazard note saying so (`.engramdb/memories/invoices-finalize-is-not-idempotent_\u2026md`): \"Calling it twice double-posts. Never add retries around it.\" The code agrees: `src/billing/invoices.py:22` sends nothing the ledger could use to spot a duplicate.\n\nThe risky case is a timeout or connection reset that happens after the ledger has already recorded the posting. We get an error, retry, and the invoice is posted twice. `finalize_once()` doesn't catch this, because `ledger_ref` is only set after a successful response, so it stays empty when the response is lost.\n\n**Options:**\n\n1. **Idempotency key (best, if the ledger supports it).** Send a stable key per invoice, such as an `Idempotency-Key: invoice-<id>` header, and retry on network errors. The ledger then ignores duplicates. Someone needs to confirm the ledger API supports this. Nothing in this repo says either way.\n2. **Retry only connect failures.** Retry `requests.exceptions.ConnectTimeout` and connection-refused errors, where the request never reached the server, with up to 3 attempts and backoff. Don't retry read timeouts or resets after sending. This is safe today but won't cover every network error you're seeing.\n3. **Check, then retry.** On a doubtful failure, ask the ledger whether a posting already exists for this invoice before retrying. This needs a lookup endpoint, which I can't see here.\n\nOption 2 is the only one I can build safely with what's in the repo. Should I go ahead with it, or can you check whether the ledger accepts idempotency keys so we can do option 1?"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 682, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25363, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 682}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5034ee0e-c300-47d7-998a-8b571678ea0c", "uuid": "ab197d3f-01d8-4d86-8c5f-7f38401d56b9", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T15:43:40.917Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbmqEnvkM4QY8hQh9qvb"}
